SCOPE
-----

This licence applies to the files in this repository that do NOT carry their
own copyright and licence notice.

A great deal of this repository is third-party code, bundled so the core can
be built and used from a single checkout. Every such file or directory carries
the copyright and licence notice of its own authors, and those terms — not
this licence — govern it. Nothing here claims copyright over that work, grants
rights in it, or relicenses it. THIRD-PARTY.md enumerates the bundled
components and their licences.

Two consequences worth stating plainly rather than leaving to be discovered:

  * This repository as a whole is NOT distributable under the MIT licence
    alone. It bundles LGPL-2.1 components — including ArduinoCore-API, on
    which the core is built, and several libraries derived from the ESP8266
    and arduino-pico cores — whose terms continue to apply to the combined
    distribution.

  * The vendor SDK under system/ is supplied by Nanjing Qinheng
    Microelectronics (WCH) under terms that restrict its use to WCH-made
    microcontrollers. It is not a free-software licence and cannot be treated
    as one.

If you are reusing individual files, check the header of the file you are
taking. If it has no notice, this licence covers it.

